---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title={"RITdb Rich Interactive Test Database | Roos Instruments"}
  description={"RITdb is Rich Interactive Test Database, the latest SEMI standard to replace STDF.  Cassini implements RITdb natively."}
  active={["nav-products"]}>
        <!-- ==========================
    	BREADCRUMB - START
    =========================== -->
        <section class="breadcrumb-wrapper">
            <div class="container">
                <h2>RITdb - Rich Interactive Test Database</h2>
                <ol class="breadcrumb">
                    <li><a href="/index.html">Home</a></li>
                    <li><a href="/products.html">Products</a></li>
                    <li><a href="/software.html">Software</a></li>
                </ol>
            </div>
        </section>
        <!-- ==========================
    	BREADCRUMB - END
    =========================== -->
        <section id="content" class="roosC container">
            <div class="row">
                <h1>Data Infrastructure for Backend Smart Manufacturing</h1>
                <img id="UserInterface" class="full-page" src="images/ritdb-data-waterfall2.jpg"
                    alt="RITdb Datalog Waterfall" style="top: -30px;">
            </div>
            <div class="row">
                <div class="col-sm-10 col-sm-offset-1">
                    <p class="main">
                        Streaming RITdb is a flexible, extendable test data logging infrastructure with the ability to
                        collect and act upon data in real-time. RITdb works as both a container (STDF replacement) and a
                        bi-directional streaming format to enable real-time operational control for adaptive test and
                        data analytics. It is built on open-source <abbr title="internet-of-things">IoT</abbr> standards
                        for simple intergration with your current Big Data private cloud infrastructure.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div class="col-sm-10 col-sm-offset-1">
                    <ul style="padding-right: 20px;">
                        <li>Bi-Directional Streaming and Storage via MQTT (<abbr
                                title="Open Source Software">OSS</abbr>)</li>
                        <li>Distributed "data lake" model for Adaptive Test and Big Data</li>
                        <li>Extensible and Works in Parallel with Legacy Formats (like <abbr
                                title="Standard Test Data Format">STDF</abbr>)</li>
                        <li>Security and Integrity with Crypto Signatures</li>

                        <li class="hidden-xs" style="margin-left: 55%;">
                            <a title="RITdb Overview Presentation 2021" target="_new"
                                href="/pdf/SmartManufacturing-RITdbOverview-210429.pdf">
                                RITdb Overview Presentation &raquo;
                            </a>
                        </li>
                        <li style="margin-left: 100px;" class="visible-xs">
                            <a title="Learn about Roos Cassini ATE (brochure)"
                                href="/pdf/SmartManufacturing-RITdbOverview-210429.pdf">
                                Learn More &raquo;
                            </a>
                        </li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </div> <!-- .row -->

            <hr class="space">
            <div class="row">
                <h2 style="position: relative; z-index: 1;">Revolutionary New Data Standard</h2>

                <div class="col-md-8">
                    <div class="embed-responsive embed-responsive-16by9"><iframe width="560" height="315" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/7PmcFtE505c"
                        title="RITdb - YouTube video player" frameborder="0" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture"
                        referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" allowfullscreen></iframe></div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-3">
                    <p>
                        Rich Interactive Test Database (RITdb) is the next generation file format for storing and
                        processing testdata. Cassini systems natively support RITdb.
                    </p>
                    <a href="/web/stdfTranslatorV86.zip" class="btn btn-primary"><i class="fa-solid fa-download"></i>Download
                        stdf Translator v86</a>
                    <p>
                        To launch GUI, double click on stdf7.jar. (requires Java, <a
                            href="https://ninite.com/adoptjavax11/" rel="nofollow">Win10</a>)
                    </p>
                    <p>
                       RITdb Translator <a href="https://github.com/RITdb/ritdb.Translator/tree/master/src/ritdb">Java Source</a>
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        <a href="https://store-us.semi.org/products/semi-002-introduction-to-ritdb-semi-e183-implementation-on-a-test-floor" rel="external">
                            <img src="/images/semi-logo.webp" width="150" alt="SEMI" style="width: 150px;" /> SEMI Introduction to RITdb (SEMI E183) implementation on a test floor.</a> 
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="row">
                <h2>Newsworthy Innovation</h2>
                <p>
                    Read more about the impact of RITdb on the industry.
                </p>
                <div class="col-sm-10">
                    <blockquote>
                        Demand for more and better data for test is driving a major standards effort, paving the way for
                        one of most significant changes in data formats in years.<br>
                        There is good reason for this shift. Data from device testing is becoming a critical element in
                        test program decisions regarding limits and flows. This is true for everything from automotive
                        and medical components to complex, heterogeneous devices such as processors used in servers or
                        smart phones. And increasingly, all of these devices are expected to function flawlessly for
                        longer periods of time, which can be more than a decade for automotive, industrial, and medical
                        applications.
                    </blockquote>
                    <span>- Ann Meixner</span><br>
                    <span> <a href="https://semiengineering.com/new-data-format-boosts-test-analytics/" target="_new">
                            New Data Format Boosts Test Analytics</a> article in Semiconductor Engineering, Sept 2020</span>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="row">
                <h2 style="position: relative; z-index: 1;">SEMICON West 2022 Workshop</h2>

                <div class="col-md-7">
                    <div class="embed-responsive embed-responsive-16by9"><iframe width="560" height="315" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/sQ6HL1P_3JM"
                        title="SEMICON West 2022 Workshop - YouTube video player" frameborder="0"
                        allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture"
                        referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" allowfullscreen></iframe></div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-5">
                    <p>
                        Highlights:
                    <ul>
                        <li>
                            0:00-1:07 - Overview
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            1:07-1:35 - <a href="https://youtu.be/sQ6HL1P_3JM?t=4045" title="Demos">Demos</a>
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            1:35-2:12 - <a href="https://youtu.be/sQ6HL1P_3JM?t=4045"
                                title="RITdb Client Implementation">RITdb Client Implementation</a>
                        </li>
                    </ul>
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <hr class="space">
            <span class="pull-right"><a href="/software.html" class="link pull-right">Learn More about Software
                    &raquo;</a></span>
        </section>
</Base>
